title: $:/plugins/tiddlywiki/forms/readme

A configuration-driven engine for building navigation, overviews, guided editing and spreadsheet exports over a wiki whose structure is already expressed in tags and fields.

!! The idea

An //operation// is a named function from a tiddler to a value or a list. Export columns, group keys and tree relations are all the same thing: a function name. Two reports that select different tiddlers and show different columns are therefore the same code with different data — no second code path.

!! What it provides

|!Feature |!Usage |
|`forms-tree` |`<$transclude $variable="forms-tree" roots="<filter>" children="<fn>"/>` — a cycle-safe collapsible tree over a relation function |
|`forms-group` |`<$transclude $variable="forms-group" set="<titles>" groups="<fn> <fn>" sorts="<fn> <fn>"/>` — a collapsible group-by tree; reordering `groups` is the only difference between grouping variants |
|`forms-grouped-view` |`<<forms-grouped-view views state setlabel orderlabel rowlabel>>` — one picker chooses //what// to look at, a second chooses //how// it is grouped, both from a JSON catalogue |
|`forms-form` |`<<forms-form def state>>` — guided creation from a definition: which inputs to ask for, a template for the title, filters for the tags and fields, a tiddler to seed the body |
|`forms-edit` |`<<forms-edit def state>>` — the same definition run backwards over an existing tiddler, keeping tags the form does not manage and renaming with relink when the title changes |
|`forms-todo-*` |Which members of a population still owe an item for a period, and whether what they filed is real |
|`forms-export` |`<<forms-export set columns filename limit caption rowlabel>>` — a download link plus a preview table |
|`forms-csv` |`[<filter>] +[forms-csv[<column-spec>]]` — CSV with a leading UTF-8 BOM, so spreadsheet software reads it as UTF-8 |
|`forms-datauri` |`[<text>] +[forms-datauri[<mime-type>]]` — wraps a string for an `<a download>` link |
|`fold` / `forms-search` |`[<titles>forms-search:title[<query>]]` — diacritic-insensitive search, so a query typed without accents still finds the accented text |

Each feature's own tiddler documents it in full; open the plugin's contents tab to read them.

!! Configuring it

This plugin carries mechanism only: it defines no selectors, no columns and no vocabulary of its own, and contains no strings specific to any one deployment. A companion configuration plugin supplies those as shadow tiddlers, and users override anything with ordinary tiddlers of the same title. Deleting such an override restores the default.

Two config slots ship here with neutral defaults for a configuration layer to replace: [[$:/config/forms/labels]] (button and warning captions) and [[$:/config/forms/fold-map]] (letters that Unicode normalisation cannot fold on its own).

A JSON config tiddler may carry a `"documentation"` key: wikitext, wikified in place above the editor when the tiddler is opened, so a configuration layer's own overrides — an unfamiliar letter table, an otherwise-bare `{}` — are not left to speak for themselves. It can `[[link]]` to whatever explains it. The key is reserved by convention: a consumer that iterates a JSON tiddler's own keys (`fold-map`, for one) must skip it.

A configuration layer must declare a higher `plugin-priority` than this plugin, or its overrides will not win: TiddlyWiki unpacks plugins in priority order and falls back to alphabetical order by title.

Because reset-by-deletion depends on the defaults staying pristine, nothing here writes to its own configuration tiddlers at runtime.
